project-based now has a CGI trailer  gameplay footage impressions from a 30  minute demo and most importantly a name  let's talk about blood-borne and let's  start with the gameplay  according to Massa Akiyama gawe from  japan studios the combat in blood-borne  is based on intense life-threatening  battles think about how you fight in the  souls games you're encouraged to take  out enemies methodically but you're also  encouraged towards a passive sort of  block weight and attack when the enemy  is open style of combat you probe for  weaknesses and you exploit them  blood-borne is taking the strategic  element from the soul series but  applying it in a different way in  blood-borne there's going to be a  transition to a quicker more offensive  and active combat style with close range  weapons and guns in the soul series  you're tentatively exploring the level  to make it through but in blood-borne  we've been told that we'll be under a  more constant threat and attack with  every fight being a scrap to survive in  this game it sounds like it will be  preferable to take out enemies quickly  before you can get overwhelmed an  offensive approach to combat rather than  the defensive one we see in souls games  that sounds really good in terms of  story blood-borne takes place in yharnam  an ancient forgotten city cursed with a  horrible endemic illness in light of the  name blood-borne it seems very much  inspired by the era of the Black Plague  except this illness it's a little  different rumors flying around suggest  that the blood-borne plague is turning  men into beasts another rumor is that  you become more beasts like as you take  the blood of your enemies which could be  some sort of twist on the hollow human  form mechanic over the years many  hopeless and afflicted people have made  pilgrimages to Yanam in search of a cure  you are one of these travelers  navigating this gothic horrific City  fighting off the endless deranged  nightmarish creatures that creep from  the shadows we've only seen one  protagonist so far but it's just like  the other Souls games you know there's  always that one character who is a  symbol of that game because according to  firm itsu character customization is  confirmed in the same article they note  that it's going to be very similar  mechanically to a Souls game with the UI  apparently more or less identical to the  Souls UI at this point there will also  be online elements and a few in  have also mentioned that a four-player  co-op is an emphasis of this game  perhaps being more play with a friend  friendly than previous titles in a  previous screenshot we saw blood flying  through the air in a manner reminiscent  of a soul in the later video footage the  protag was becoming more and more  drenched in blood and finally in the new  trailer the protagonist is cutting a  beast purposefully with his saw cleaver  there's this emphasis on blood and I'm  sure it'll play into the game  mechanically somehow just like we had  souls before this might mean that we  gain something from blood and to think  when we heard that Miyazaki was being  moved to a different project he said  that he wanted to work on a lighter  hearted game I think he might have been  messing with us permits who notes that  the game has been in development since  the release of the artorias of the abyss  DLC another interesting thing to note is  that we haven't seen any of the footage  from the gameplay leaked a little while  ago but a 30 minute gameplay preview was  shown behind closed doors at e3 and I  have the details for you here as I  mentioned before the game takes place  inside a city environments will be  densely layer as we dash through  alleyways across rooftops within houses  ascending stairs and Criss crossing  through adjoining rooms many paths will  be available and many will lead to the  same point so I imagine if you were a  fan of the complex level design in Dark  Souls where levels twist around on each  other and it sounds like you're going to  be a fan of this and as I thought about  the close-range combat that will take  place inside houses it reminded me of  the so clever we've seen within footage  so far the ability to transform it into  a close-range weapon or a long-range  weapon will really help you depending on  whether you're fighting in a closed  corridor or in an open courtyard for  example we've also been told that we  should expect to see an entire class of  transforming weapons as well these  weapons will have different properties  depending on the form they take for  example the soul Cleaver will be able to  crush enemy guards in its shortened form  they should add a really good layer of  depth and versatility to the combat you  might also be wondering about guns and  another surprising thing that we learned  was that guns are actually intended to  be more commonly a close-range weapon  that will help you the offensive  versatility  really what a lot of this has been about  it's been about giving you this  offensive versatility that will allow  you to cut down enemies more effectively  in one of the gameplay previews a player  was shown stunning an enemy with a  gunshot and then performing a finishing  critical attack Miyazaki has apparently  said that you cannot play this game the  same way you would play demon souls you  can't just stand back and bait enemies  until they're open no in this game you  have to take a more active approach to  combat or you risk getting overwhelmed  by a more constant assault so think  about it you actually have to cut down  enemies before they overwhelm you  because it sounds like they might be  coming at you at a more constant rate  keeping this in mind it makes sense that  we should be holding a gun in our  offhand instead of a shield and I can  see this shield 'less offense focused  shift being the biggest difference  between the Soul series and blood-borne  the main enemy in yharnam are the humans  turned beasts by the infection plaguing  the place but that's not all you should  expect to see in the footage enemies  were said to be hiding in the shadows  ready to jump out at you and join the  assault of other enemies a viewer  described mutilated crow like enemies  hopping towards the player and there's  this abundance of lycanthropes and  beasts seen so far the difficulty is  said to be similar to Demon Souls and  Miyazaki says to expect the same  satisfying feeling you get from  overcoming adversity in a Souls game to  me  the discussion is less about difficulty  and more about the different flavors  strategic gameplay we'll be seeing and  I'm really curious to see how well  faster paced combat will be developed  within the framework of a Souls game  blood-borne is being targeted for a  spring release in 2015 exclusive to the  PlayStation 4 platform it's exclusive  because Sony owns the demon souls IP and  actually co-developed this with From  Software and their own Sony Japan  studios similar to what they did back in  the day when they helped create Demon  Souls the team is aiming to get the game  at 30 frames per second at 1080p I've  listed a lot of sources in the  description and I really want you to  check them out to support the people who  translated articles and attended these  behind-the-scenes events subscribe to  hear more about blood-borne news when it  drops  you guys next time
 

